{"seq":33,"slug":"negotiation-theory","title":"谈判理论与实践","stage":"DONE","category":"management","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory","rating":{"composite":3.94,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":4,"coverage":3.75,"positioning":4,"strategic":4},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"introHtml":"<h1 id=\"谈判理论与实践\">谈判理论与实践</h1><p>谈判无处不在——从薪酬协商到商业并购，从国际外交到团队资源分配。多数人凭直觉谈判，结果往往是双方都不满意的妥协。Harvard Negotiation Project 四十余年的研究表明，超过 70% 的专业谈判产出次优协议，而结构化方法能显著改善结果。本 hub 从理论根基出发，系统构建谈判的认知框架与实操能力。</p>\n<h2 id=\"本-hub-与兄弟-hub-的分工\">本 hub 与兄弟 hub 的分工</h2><p>本 hub <strong>聚焦理论深度</strong>——博弈论模型、心理学机制、策略体系的底层逻辑。兄弟 hub <a href=\"../negotiation-skills/\">谈判技巧</a> 侧重<strong>可立即上手的操作层</strong>：准备清单、阶段话术、跨文化礼仪。两者的关系类似&quot;为什么这样做&quot;与&quot;具体怎么做&quot;：本 hub 提供决策依据，兄弟 hub 提供执行动作。</p>\n<p>与 <a href=\"../critical-thinking-decision/\">批判性思维与决策</a> 的交集在于认知偏误和决策框架——该 hub 讲通用思维工具，本 hub 将这些工具<strong>特化到对抗性互动场景</strong>中，分析对手行为、评估信息不对称、管理情绪干扰。</p>\n<h2 id=\"推荐学习路径\">推荐学习路径</h2><p><strong>路径 A（系统学习者）：</strong> 按章节顺序从基础理论 → 策略体系 → 心理学 → 实战应用，逐层递进。适合希望建立完整谈判知识体系的读者。</p>\n<p><strong>路径 B（实战导向者）：</strong> 先读第四章实战应用获取框架感，再回第一章补理论基础，最后深入策略与心理学章节。适合有谈判经验但缺乏系统化认知的读者。</p>\n<p><strong>路径 C（特定问题驱动）：</strong> 直接跳到对应章节——遇到&quot;对方不讲理&quot;的困境读心理学章节；需要评估是否接受报价读 BATNA 与博弈论；准备重要谈判读准备框架。</p>\n<h2 id=\"前置知识\">前置知识</h2><p>无硬性前置要求。以下背景有助于加速理解：基本的概率直觉（理解期望值）、对博弈论术语的初步印象（Nash 均衡、囚徒困境）、以及至少一次真实的谈判经历（无论结果如何）。如果完全没有谈判经验，建议先浏览兄弟 hub 的谈判阶段概览，建立场景感后再回来。</p>\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"foundations","title":"谈判基础理论","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/foundations","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"principled-negotiation","title":"哈佛原则谈判法","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/foundations/principled-negotiation"},{"seq":2,"slug":"batna-and-zopa","title":"BATNA 与谈判协议区","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/foundations/batna-and-zopa"},{"seq":3,"slug":"game-theory-foundations","title":"博弈论与谈判基础","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/foundations/game-theory-foundations"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"strategies","title":"谈判策略体系","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/strategies","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"distributive-negotiation","title":"分配式谈判策略","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/strategies/distributive-negotiation"},{"seq":2,"slug":"integrative-negotiation","title":"整合式谈判策略","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/strategies/integrative-negotiation"},{"seq":3,"slug":"mixed-strategy-framework","title":"混合策略框架","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/strategies/mixed-strategy-framework"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"psychology","title":"谈判心理学","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/psychology","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"tactical-empathy","title":"战术同理心","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/psychology/tactical-empathy"},{"seq":2,"slug":"cognitive-biases","title":"认知偏误与锚定效应","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/psychology/cognitive-biases"},{"seq":3,"slug":"emotional-regulation","title":"情绪管理与压力控制","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/psychology/emotional-regulation"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"practice","title":"谈判实战应用","docCount":3,"url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/practice","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"preparation-framework","title":"谈判准备框架","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/practice/preparation-framework"},{"seq":2,"slug":"communication-techniques","title":"沟通技术体系","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/practice/communication-techniques"},{"seq":3,"slug":"multi-party-negotiation","title":"多方谈判与联盟动力学","url":"/l-doc-books/h/management/negotiation-theory/practice/multi-party-negotiation"}]}]}